      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/carpenter_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Carpenter emerged as a small settlement in 1907 during a wave of homesteading across the vast Wyoming plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/carpenter_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Carpenter served as a key rail stop on the Chicago, Burlington and Quincy Railroad to transport wheat and livestock.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/carpenter_wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Carpenter sits at an elevation of five thousand four hundred forty feet in southeastern Wyoming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
